    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. What about the cost though? I heard flying can sometimes be way cheaper if you book in advance. Is there a significant price difference if i'm booking for a single traveler, or does the transit to/from the airports end up making the trains more cost-effective anyway?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a single traveler, the price difference can vary widely based on how far in advance you book both tickets and the specific fare class you choose. While flights can be cheap with advance booking, factoring in airport transfers—which can add significant time and local transport costs—often makes the Shinkansen the more cost-effective choice for this itinerary. Consider purchasing a Japan Rail Pass if you plan multiple long-distance journeys to see if it offers better overall value than individual tickets.",
      "source": "target",
